{"status": "ok", "message-type": "work-list", "message-version": "1.0.0", "message": {"facets": {}, "total-results": 152867, "items": [{"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 9, 9]], "date-time": "2026-09-09T15:22:55Z", "timestamp": 1788967375824, "version": "build-2803163510"}, "publisher-location": "San Diego, California, USA", "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "Neural Information Processing Systems Foundation, Inc. (NeurIPS)", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "published-print": {"date-parts": [[2024]]}, "DOI": "10.52202/079017-2866", "type": "proceedings-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2025, 11, 3]], "date-time": "2025-11-03T11:20:56Z", "timestamp": 1762168856000}, "page": "90277-90317", "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 10, "title": ["Mind's Eye of LLMs: Visualization-of-Thought Elicits Spatial Reasoning in Large Language Models"], "prefix": "10.52202", "author": [{"given": "Wenshan", "family": "Wu", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Shaoguang", "family": "Mao", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Yadong", "family": "Zhang", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Yan", "family": "Xia", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Li", "family": "Dong", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Lei", "family": "Cui", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Furu", "family": "Wei", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}], "member": "29733", "event": {"name": "Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems 37", "theme": "38th Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS 2024)", "location": "Vancouver, BC, Canada", "acronym": "NeurIPS 2024", "number": "37", "start": {"date-parts": [[2024, 12, 10]]}, "end": {"date-parts": [[2024, 12, 15]]}}, "container-title": ["Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems 37"], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2026, 6, 19]], "date-time": "2026-06-19T15:42:53Z", "timestamp": 1781883773000}, "score": 64.2919, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "http://www.proceedings.com/079017-2866.html"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2024]]}, "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.52202/079017-2866", "published": {"date-parts": [[2024]]}}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 8, 14]], "date-time": "2026-08-14T15:00:28Z", "timestamp": 1786719628780, "version": "build-2736575974"}, "posted": {"date-parts": [[2024]]}, "group-title": "SSRN", "reference-count": 4, "publisher": "Elsevier BV", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "abstract": "<jats:p>Do Large Language Models have cognitive abilities? &lt;br&gt;Do Large Language Models have understanding? Is the correct recognition of verbal contexts or visual objects, based on pre-learning on a large training dataset, a manifestation of the ability to solve cognitive tasks? &lt;br&gt;Or is any LLM just a statistical approximator that compiles averaged texts from its huge dataset close to the specified prompts?&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The answers to these questions require rigorous formal definitions of the cognitive concepts of \u201dknowledge\u201d, \u201dunderstanding\u201d and related terms.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.2139/ssrn.4819603", "type": "posted-content", "created": {"date-parts": [[2024, 5, 7]], "date-time": "2024-05-07T16:36:38Z", "timestamp": 1715099798000}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["Reasoning AI (RAI), Large Language Models (LLMs) and Cognition"], "prefix": "10.2139", "author": [{"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8874-7939", "authenticated-orcid": true, "given": "Victor", "family": "Senkevich", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}], "member": "78", "reference": [{"key": "ref1", "author": "D Kahneman", "year": "2011"}, {"key": "ref2", "volume": "5", "author": "C Peirce", "year": "1934", "journal-title": "Collected papers of Charles Sanders Peirce"}, {"key": "ref3", "author": "V Senkevich", "journal-title": "Existence and Perception as the basis of AGI (Artificial General Intelligence)"}, {"key": "ref4", "author": "N Wiener", "journal-title": "The Human Use of Human Beings"}], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2026, 8, 14]], "date-time": "2026-08-14T14:12:23Z", "timestamp": 1786716743000}, "score": 42.56736, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://www.ssrn.com/abstract=4819603"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2024]]}, "references-count": 4, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.4819603", "relation": {"has-preprint": [{"id-type": "doi", "id": "10.31219/osf.io/65rkw", "asserted-by": "object"}, {"id-type": "doi", "id": "10.36227/techrxiv.171560715.55982164/v1", "asserted-by": "object"}]}, "published": {"date-parts": [[2024]]}, "subtype": "preprint"}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 6, 3]], "date-time": "2026-06-03T21:01:07Z", "timestamp": 1780520467192, "version": "3.54.1"}, "posted": {"date-parts": [[2024, 5, 13]]}, "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers (IEEE)", "license": [{"start": {"date-parts": [[2024, 5, 13]], "date-time": "2024-05-13T00:00:00Z", "timestamp": 1715558400000}, "content-version": "unspecified", "delay-in-days": 0, "URL": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}], "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "abstract": "<jats:p>Do Large Language Models have cognitive abilities? Do Large Language Models have understanding? Is the correct recognition of verbal contexts or visual objects, based on pre-learning on a large training dataset, a manifestation of the ability to solve cognitive tasks? Or is any LLM just a statistical approximator that compiles averaged texts from its huge dataset close to the specified prompts? The answers to these questions require rigorous formal definitions of the cognitive concepts of \"knowledge\", \"understanding\" and related terms.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.36227/techrxiv.171560715.55982164/v1", "type": "posted-content", "created": {"date-parts": [[2024, 5, 13]], "date-time": "2024-05-13T09:32:41Z", "timestamp": 1715592761000}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["Reasoning AI (RAI), Large Language Models (LLMs) and Cognition"], "prefix": "10.36227", "author": [{"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8874-7939", "authenticated-orcid": false, "given": "Victor", "family": "Senkevich", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}], "member": "263", "link": [{"URL": "https://www.techrxiv.org/doi/pdf/10.36227/techrxiv.171560715.55982164/v1", "content-type": "unspecified", "content-version": "vor", "intended-application": "similarity-checking"}], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2026, 6, 3]], "date-time": "2026-06-03T20:06:55Z", "timestamp": 1780517215000}, "score": 43.27446, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://www.techrxiv.org/doi/full/10.36227/techrxiv.171560715.55982164/v1"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2024, 5, 13]]}, "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.36227/techrxiv.171560715.55982164/v1", "relation": {"is-preprint-of": [{"id-type": "doi", "id": "10.2139/ssrn.4819603", "asserted-by": "subject"}]}, "published": {"date-parts": [[2024, 5, 13]]}, "subtype": "preprint"}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 6, 12]], "date-time": "2026-06-12T16:06:02Z", "timestamp": 1781280362797, "version": "3.54.1"}, "posted": {"date-parts": [[2025, 9, 11]]}, "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers (IEEE)", "license": [{"start": {"date-parts": [[2025, 9, 11]], "date-time": "2025-09-11T00:00:00Z", "timestamp": 1757548800000}, "content-version": "unspecified", "delay-in-days": 0, "URL": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}], "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "abstract": "<jats:p>Recent progress in reasoning with large language models (LLMs) has been driven by prompting strategies such as Chain-of-Thought (CoT), Tree-of-Thought (ToT), Graph-of-Thought (GoT), and Hypergraph-of-Thought (HoT). Each introduces a powerful but fixed paradigm, forcing practitioners to manually select how a model should reason. In contrast, humans adapt their reasoning style-choosing between linear deduction, branching exploration, or relational inference depending on the task. We introduce Meta-of-Thought (MoT), a unifying controller that enables LLMs to reason about reasoning. MoT dynamically selects the most appropriate paradigm-CoT for arithmetic, ToT for planning, GoT for relational queries, and HoT for multimodal or scientific reasoning-closing the gap between fixed strategies and adaptive human cognition. A minimal rule-based prototype using flan-t5-small shows that MoT improves flexibility and robustness compared to static prompting. We position MoT as a step toward metacognitive LLMs that not only generate thoughts, but also decide how to think, opening a path for the next generation of reasoning research.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.36227/techrxiv.175756693.33854887/v1", "type": "posted-content", "created": {"date-parts": [[2025, 9, 11]], "date-time": "2025-09-11T05:02:20Z", "timestamp": 1757566940000}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["Meta-of-Thought: Reasoning About Reasoning in Large Language Models"], "prefix": "10.36227", "author": [{"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5571-7231", "authenticated-orcid": false, "given": "Ahshanul", "family": "Haque", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [{"name": "Department of Computer Science, New Mexico Tech Socorro"}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}], "member": "263", "link": [{"URL": "https://www.techrxiv.org/doi/pdf/10.36227/techrxiv.175756693.33854887/v1", "content-type": "unspecified", "content-version": "vor", "intended-application": "similarity-checking"}], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2026, 6, 12]], "date-time": "2026-06-12T15:35:00Z", "timestamp": 1781278500000}, "score": 41.94805, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://www.techrxiv.org/doi/full/10.36227/techrxiv.175756693.33854887/v1"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2025, 9, 11]]}, "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.36227/techrxiv.175756693.33854887/v1", "published": {"date-parts": [[2025, 9, 11]]}, "subtype": "preprint"}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2025, 5, 14]], "date-time": "2025-05-14T08:04:33Z", "timestamp": 1747209873646, "version": "3.40.5"}, "posted": {"date-parts": [[2024, 5, 8]]}, "group-title": "\u041c\u0430\u0442\u0435\u043c\u0430\u0442\u0438\u043a\u0430, \u0438\u043d\u0444\u043e\u0440\u043c\u0430\u0442\u0438\u043a\u0430, \u043a\u0438\u0431\u0435\u0440\u043d\u0435\u0442\u0438\u043a\u0430", "reference-count": 4, "publisher": "NPG Publishing", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "abstract": "<jats:p>Do Large Language Models have cognitive abilities? \r\nDo Large Language Models have understanding? \r\nIs the correct recognition of verbal contexts or visual objects, based on pre-learning on a large training dataset, a manifestation of the ability to solve cognitive tasks? \r\nOr is any LLM just a statistical approximator that compiles averaged texts from its huge dataset close to the specified prompts?\r\nThe answers to these questions require rigorous formal definitions of the cognitive concepts of \u201dknowledge\u201d, \u201dunderstanding\u201d and related terms.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.24108/preprints-3113041", "type": "posted-content", "created": {"date-parts": [[2024, 5, 9]], "date-time": "2024-05-09T16:39:48Z", "timestamp": 1715272788000}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["Reasoning AI (RAI), Large Language Models (LLMs) and Cognition"], "prefix": "10.24108", "author": [{"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8874-7939", "authenticated-orcid": false, "given": "\u0412\u0438\u043a\u0442\u043e\u0440", "family": "\u0421\u0435\u043d\u043a\u0435\u0432\u0438\u0447", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [{"name": "Organoid AGI Project"}], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}], "member": "10196", "reference": [{"unstructured": "Kahneman, D. Thinking, Fast and Slow. Macmillan, 2011.", "key": "0"}, {"unstructured": "Peirce, C., Hartshorne, C., and Weiss, P. Collected papers of Charles Sanders Peirce. volume 5, Cambridge, MA, 1934. Harvard University Press.", "key": "1"}, {"unstructured": "Senkevich, V. Existence and Perception as the basis of AGI (Artificial General Intelligence). arXiv:2202.03155 [cs.AI], 2022.", "key": "2"}, {"unstructured": "Wiener, N. The Human Use of Human Beings: Cybernetics and Society. The Riverside Press, Cambridge, Massachusetts, 1950.", "key": "3"}], "link": [{"URL": "https://preprints.ru/files/1520", "content-type": "application/pdf", "content-version": "vor", "intended-application": "text-mining"}], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2024, 5, 9]], "date-time": "2024-05-09T16:39:48Z", "timestamp": 1715272788000}, "score": 41.221066, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://preprints.ru/article/1345"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2024, 5, 8]]}, "references-count": 4, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.24108/preprints-3113041", "published": {"date-parts": [[2024, 5, 8]]}, "subtype": "preprint"}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2025, 12, 2]], "date-time": "2025-12-02T23:51:23Z", "timestamp": 1764719483348, "version": "3.46.0"}, "posted": {"date-parts": [[2024, 5, 10]]}, "group-title": "Open Science Framework", "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "Center for Open Science", "license": [{"start": {"date-parts": [[2024, 5, 10]], "date-time": "2024-05-10T00:00:00Z", "timestamp": 171